    "id": "s05",
    "group": "samples",
    "caller": "HandleAiAgentExecutionStart",
    "description": "Answer with bash code blocks in the answer text (the reported bug)",
    "input": "[\n  {\n    \"i\": 0,\n    \"action\": \"finish\",\n    \"category\": \"finish\",\n    \"tool\": \"core\",\n    \"confidence\": 1.0,\n    \"runs\": \"1\",\n    \"delay\": \"0\",\n    \"approval_required\": false,\n    \"data_filter\": \"full\",\n    \"reason\": \"Provide clear, supportive, and exact remediation instructions and pip commands to fix the LangChain vulnerability.\",\n    \"fields\": [\n      {\n        \"key\": \"output\",\n        \"value\": \"### Remediation Guide: Fixing the LangChain Vulnerability\\n\\nLangChain has had several notable vulnerabilities historically (most notably arbitrary code execution via unsafe evaluation in modules like `PALChain` or SQL injection in early versions, e.g., CVE-2023-36258, CVE-2023-36095, CVE-2023-39659). In newer releases, LangChain has modularized its packages into `langchain`, `langchain-core`, and `langchain-community` with strict sandbox controls.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 1. Exact Upgrade Commands\\n\\nTo upgrade `langchain` and its companion libraries to the latest secure versions, run the following command in your active Python environment:\\n\\n```bash\\npip install --upgrade langchain langchain-core langchain-community\\n```\\n\\nIf your service runs in a virtual environment (recommended), ensure it is activated first:\\n```bash\\nsource /path/to/your/venv/bin/activate\\npip install --upgrade langchain langchain-core langchain-community\\n```\\n\\nIf you need to update your `requirements.txt` file automatically:\\n```bash\\npip install --upgrade langchain langchain-core langchain-community\\npip freeze | grep langchain > updated_langchain_requirements.txt\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 2. Verify the Installed Version\\n\\nRun the following command to verify that the upgraded package is active:\\n\\n```bash\\npython3 -c \\\"import langchain; print('LangChain version:', langchain.__version__)\\\"\\n```\\nOr inspect via pip:\\n```bash\\npip show langchain langchain-core\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 3. Practical Safety & Validation Steps\\n\\n1. **Restart Running Services:** Don't forget to restart your application or systemd service worker so the new package in memory is picked up:\\n   ```bash\\n   sudo systemctl restart <your-service-name>\\n   ```\\n2. **Check for Deprecated Imports:** If upgrading from `0.0.x` or early `0.1.x`, some classes may have moved to `langchain_community` or `langchain_core`. Run your test suite or check logs on startup to catch any import changes.\\n3. **Sanitize Dynamic Code Execution:** If your application uses `load_tools` with tools like `python_repl` or `pal-chain`, ensure `allow_dangerous_tools=True` is only set if strictly necessary and input is strictly validated.\"\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n]",
    "expect_success_after": [
      "HandleAiAgentExecutionStart"
    ]
  },
